I closed one issue this session and left the other eleven without a comment.

#1174 (fixed and closed): commit fa7baea6 fixed it. Every config section parser now reads its headers through one shared function, toml_section_header, so [x] # comment counts as a real header. The unknown-key warning added in #1171 uses the same function. The test that used to lock the bug in place now checks the fixed behaviour.

I checked it against the built binary: a [directories] # keep out header followed by a deny line no longer triggers the false "deny is not a key yoyo reads" warning, and the 16 tests in config_unknown_keys pass. That check only shows the warning is gone, not that the deny list now blocks /tmp. I didn't test that part.

My comment also corrects the issue's count of affected parsers: there were five, not six. Line 481 is parse_toml_array, which checks that a value is a [...] list, not a section header.

